{
  "headline": "FDA's records trace our supply to a plant classified OAI 4184 days before the posting",
  "headline_cites": ["D3"],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "FDA first posted the sufentanil citrate shortage on 2022-05-03 and it remains current as of 2026-10-21.",
      "cites": ["E19", "E17", "E18"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The product used at both Corvale sites carries NDC 00409338221 and is labeled by Hospira, Inc. at FEI 1021343.",
      "cites": ["E1", "E2", "E16"]
    },
    {
      "text": "FDA inspected that plant on 2010-01-19 and classified it OAI, with the classification known on 2010-04-19 — 4184 days before the shortage posting.",
      "cites": ["E6", "D3"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Additional OAI inspections occurred on 2011-06-17 and 2011-08-04, and a Warning Letter was issued on 2010-04-12.",
      "cites": ["E8", "E10", "E15"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The most recent inspection of the plant was on 2025-02-07 and was classified NAI.",
      "cites": ["E16"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Corvale East has 7.1 days of supply on hand and Corvale General has 16.1 days.",
      "cites": ["D1", "D2"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The top-ranked option is to transfer 17 vials from Corvale General to Corvale East, which would leave the sender with 14 days and bring the receiver to 9 days; this requires pharmacy director approval and a DEA Form 222 or CSOS order for the Schedule II product.",
      "cites": ["D5"]
    }
  ]
}
